    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0361" n="351" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg351"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.20293/7–1248: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-12T19:00:00-04:00">July 12, 1948—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1018. Telegram Jul 6<anchor n="83" xml:id="d267-f1"/> ComNavPortFac
                        Shanghai<anchor n="84" xml:id="d267-f2"/> to ComNav-WesPae<anchor n="85"
                        xml:id="d267-f3"/> repeated CNO<anchor n="86" xml:id="d267-f4"/> for info
                    reports increasing number USSR citizens proceeding Taiwan recent weeks including
                    persons known have connection with Soviet espionage agents. Telegram further
                    states according Chinese intelligence these persons ordered report <pb
                        facs="0362" n="352" xml:id="pg352"/> AAG activities and while Chinese
                    security organs endeavoring maintain close surveillance not believed it will be
                    sufficient.</p>
                <p>Emb requested discuss foregoing informally with FonOff and express Dept’s concern
                    this situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d267-f1" n="83" xml:id="d267-f1-content">
                <p>Not found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f2" n="84" xml:id="d267-f2-content">
                <p>Commander, Naval Port Facilities, Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f3" n="85" xml:id="d267-f3-content">
                <p>Commander. U. S. Naval Forces in the Western Pacific.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f4" n="86" xml:id="d267-f4-content">
                <p>Chief of Naval Operations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
